n; the unread count matches; mark_read is   idempotent; a notification for another account is never returned.CONSTRAINTS:- Never notify an account about something it cannot see.- A notification is a pointer, not a copy. If the underlying item is gone, the link should fail  gracefully rather than showing stale content.VERIFY:- The notification tests pass.- Mentioning a user in chat produces a badge update without a refresh.- Full suite >= 621 passed, 0 failed.- ruff clean.COMMIT: feat(app): add notification centre and triggers```---Prompt 15 — P2.4: Close out P2```PREAMBLEGOAL: Prove P2 and close the phase.CHANGES:1. tests/helix_codex_app/test_messaging_isolation.py — an account in tenant A can never read a   conversation, message, or notification belonging to tenant B.2. tests/helix_codex_app/test_sse_isolation.py — the conversation stream refuses a non-member; the   notification stream only emits events for the owning account.3. tests/helix_codex_app/test_notification_triggers.py — each wired trigger fires once and only once.4. Update helix_codex_app/agents.md and repomap.md.CONSTRAINTS:- Tests and ledger updates only. No new features.VERIFY:- The three new test modules pass.- Full suite >= 621 passed, 0 failed.- ruff clean.COMMIT: test(app): prove messaging and notification isolation, close phase p2```---7. PHASE P3 — Documents, KB/SOP, tasksPrompt 16 — P3.1: Documents and the block editor```PREAMBLEGOAL: Documents made of blocks, editable in place, with the edits saved as you type.CONTEXT: The parent already models this: server/models/node.py has NodeKind.DOCUMENT andNodeKind.BLOCK, and its docstring says chat, docs, tasks, and workflows are the same object seenthrough four lenses. Follow that. A document is a row plus an ordered list of blocks. The editor isplain contenteditable; the autosave is a debounced HTMX post. No rich-text library, no CRDT.CHANGES:1. helix_codex_app/modules/docs/repository.py and service.py — create_document, get_document,   list_documents(account, filters), update_block, insert_block, delete_block, reorder_blocks,   archive_document. Every write calls record_node() with kind document or block.2. helix_codex_app/modules/docs/router.py — GET /app/docs, GET /app/docs/{id}, POST /app/api/documents,   GET /app/api/documents/{id}, PUT /app/api/documents/{id}/blocks/{block_id},   POST /app/api/documents/{id}/blocks.3. helix_codex_app/templates/partials/doc_editor.html — a block list where each block is a   contenteditable element that posts its content on blur and on a 1.5 second debounce. Show a small   saved indicator.4. helix_codex_app/templates/docs.html — the document list with a create button and search.5. Tests: creating a document creates one node; editing a block updates it and creates one node; a   block from another document cannot be edited through this document's route; blocks keep their   order after a reorder.CONSTRAINTS:- Single writer per block. No collaborative editing in v1. If two people edit the same block, the  later write wins and both are recorded.- The editor must work without JavaScript for reading; only saving needs HTMX.VERIFY:- Create a document, type in three blocks, reload, and confirm the content survived.- Full suite >= 621 passed, 0 failed.- ruff clean.COMMIT: feat(app): add block documents and inline editor```---Prompt 17 — P3.2: Versions and the knowledge base```PREAMBLEGOAL: Document versions you can look at and restore, and a knowledge base view that gathers SOPs inone place.CONTEXT: Restore has to be safe: restoring an old version creates a new version, it never rewriteshistory. The knowledge base is a filtered view of documents marked as KB or SOP, not a separatestore. Managers and owners publish; everyone reads.CHANGES:1. Extend helix_codex_app/modules/docs/service.py — snapshot_version(document_id) writing the whole   block list into document_versions, list_versions(document_id), get_version(version_id),   restore_version(document_id, version_no) which writes a new version whose content equals the old   one and records the restore in the audit trail.2. Add a doc_type field usage: note, sop, kb, policy. Only a manager or owner may set doc_type to sop   or policy, enforced in the service.3. helix_codex_app/modules/docs/router.py — POST /app/api/documents/{id}/versions,   GET /app/api/documents/{id}/versions, POST /app/api/documents/{id}/versions/{n}/restore,   GET /app/kb with a type filter.4. helix_codex_app/templates/kb.html — a searchable list grouped by type, with the SOPs first.5. Tests: restoring version 2 of a document with 4 versions produces version 5 with version 2's   content; an employee cannot set doc_type to policy; a version snapshot is immutable.CONSTRAINTS:- Restore appends. It never deletes or rewrites a version row.- A KB or SOP document is visible to everyone in the tenant; a note is visible to its owner and to  managers.VERIFY:- The version tests pass.- Restore a document through the UI and confirm the block content reverts and a new version appears.- Full suite >= 621 passed, 0 failed.- ruff clean.COMMIT: feat(app): add document versions and the knowledge base```---Prompt 18 — P3.3: Tasks```PREAMBLEGOAL: Tasks with a board, assignment, due dates, and comments.CONTEXT: Tasks are the other half of the daily loop: chat tells you something, a task makes ithappen. Assignment fires a notification, which P2 already built. Keep the statuses to three: open,doing, done.CHANGES:1. helix_codex_app/modules/tasks/repository.py and service.py — create_task, get_task, list_tasks   (account, filters), update_task, set_status, assign, add_comment. Creating or assigning a task   fires the notification from P2. Every write calls record_node() with kind task.2. helix_codex_app/modules/tasks/router.py — GET /app/tasks, GET /app/tasks/{id}, POST /app/api/tasks,   PUT /app/api/tasks/{id}, POST 